       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for prescription use in adults (3,200 mg/day), and a single 1,600 mg dose is well above the typical maximum of 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **400 mg four times daily**, which is 1,600 mg/day\n- **800 mg three times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day\n- **800 mg four times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day and the maximum\n- **Something else.** If you really want 1,600 mg QID, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note.\n\nOnce you pick one, I'll enter it right away. I can also add a note, for example \"take with food\"."
